------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web -> native), from the web source read end-to-end
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data sources : useClimateHistory + useVehicles + useTranslation + useDateFormat +
               useUnits  -> bound through the P1/S8 state-holder seam
               `ClimateHistorySource` -> `ClimateHistoryUpdate` (snapshots + measurement
               + load/connection status). No HTTP in the view.
Adapter      : web `buildChartData` -> `ClimateHistoryProjectionBuilder.build`
               (drop rows without created_at||timestamp; created_at wins; SI->display
               temperature at the render boundary via `ClimateTemperature.fromSI`;
               sort ascending; latest cabin/outside scan newest-first; connectNulls).
Chart        : web Recharts <AreaChart> two gradient areas -> Swift Charts two
               AreaMark+LineMark series on one temperature axis. Cabin -> chartSeriesEnergy
               (warm amber ≈ web #f97316); Outside -> chartSeriesSpeed (blue = web #3b82f6).
States       : loading / empty / error / stale / offline / content — every branch renders
               (skeleton chrome; ContentUnavailableView empty; retry error; stale+offline
               connectivity banners + freshness chip; cached values stay visible).
i18n         : keys from source — widget.climateHistory.title "Climate History",
               .cabin "Cabin", .outside "Outside", .noData "No climate history" — plus
               registry name/description and native chrome, all via the P1/S10 facade
               (ClimateHistoryStrings table, no English literals in code). See .strings.
Registry     : id "climate-history", category "climate", default 2x4, min 2x4, max 4x40
               — encoded in `ClimateHistoryWidget.registration` + size clamp.
Telemetry    : `view.opened` surface="ClimateHistoryWidget" emitted once on start
               (P1/S11 seam, asserted by test).
A11y         : VoiceOver chart summary, combined stat labels, refresh/open labels,
               Dynamic Type fonts, reduce-motion-friendly skeleton.

