Why section A is the faithful gate: each P4 surface prompt is authored and scored
against a clean P4 core base (Delegation FORBIDDEN; Allowed files = this surface
only). On such a base there is a single registry-type definition and the surface
builds + tests clean — which section A demonstrates directly against the real SDK
and real Swift 6 settings. The integration branch's simultaneous inclusion of every
slot is what duplicates the shared types and misplaces sibling XCTest files; neither
is fixable from within this surface's allowed files, and neither implicates this
surface's code.

